# Git: no automatic commits

- **Never** run `git commit`, `git push`, `git merge`, or other commands that change git history or remotes unless the user clearly asks you to do that in their message.
- It is fine to run read-only git commands when helpful (`git status`, `git diff`, `git log`) if the user is debugging or asks.
- If the user wants changes saved, make file edits only; they will commit themselves.
